      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors William Stanard, a prominent Virginia family member who inherited part of the 1722 Octonia grant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stanardsville.org/about/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic Courthouse Square hosts the 1839 Greene County Courthouse, the 1840 Lafayette Inn, and the 1845 Gibbons Store, all on the National Register.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.stanardsville.org/about/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Stanardsville sits at the eastern foot of the Blue Ridge Mountains, offering scenic views of the Piedmont Region.",
